# Memory

`doc/memory/` holds what working on hql-demo taught that is not yet stated
where it belongs: why a case is built the way it is, and what hql did that
its book does not say. It is a staging area, not an archive.

A note stays only while it is undigested. Once what it says is in the place
that owns it, a case's section of the [README](../../README.md), an issue or
a fix in [hql](https://github.com/ewiger/hql), the note, or the part of it,
is deleted.

| Note | About |
| --- | --- |
| [greek-gods](greek-gods.hmd) | what the Greek Gods case is for, how it is built, and the hql gaps it works around |
